Subject: [PATCH v5 00/10] wifi: rtw89: monitor mode RX filter and raw frame injection fixes

This series fixes a NULL pointer dereference and an invalid rate
index on the rtw89 TX path for injected frames, makes monitor mode
receive frames that are currently dropped by the hardware RX filter,
and makes raw 802.11 frame injection work on a standalone monitor
interface.

Patches 1-2 are fixes with Fixes: tags and can be applied on their
own:
  1. drop frames without a vif instead of dereferencing NULL in
     rtw89_ops_tx() (reachable by injecting on a monitor interface
     while a station interface is up)
  2. treat the radiotap "no rate" index (-1) as signed

Patch 3 clears RX filter bits that drop frames from other BSSs while
in monitor mode.

Patches 4-9 enable injection on a standalone monitor interface:
  4. RCU protection for pure_monitor_mode_vif (no functional change)
  5. AP self role for monitor interfaces in the join info H2C
  6. resolve the vif used for monitor TX through
     pure_monitor_mode_vif
  7. management path for injected control frames, and no seq_ctrl
     read beyond the end of control frames
  8. skip traffic statistics, WoW AKM parsing, BT-coex notification,
     HE HTC and AMPDU handling for injected frames
  9. honor IEEE80211_TX_CTL_ASSIGN_SEQ and IEEE80211_TX_CTL_NO_ACK

Patch 10 restores the channel when monitor mode is restarted on the
same channel on chips without channel context support.

Open questions for Realtek:
- Patch 5: the need for RTW89_SELF_ROLE_AP was found by testing on
  RTL8852AE with firmware 0.13.36.2. Is this the intended firmware
  configuration for a monitor MAC ID, and does it hold for the other
  AX and BE chips?
- Patch 10 re-applies the channel from rtw89_ops_config(). Would you
  prefer resetting the channel state in rtw89_ops_stop() or
  re-applying it in rtw89_ops_start() instead?

Testing:
[TODO before sending: the runtime results below were obtained with
 the v4 code. Re-run scripts/verify_hardware.py on v5 and update or
 delete this note.]
- Runtime-tested only on RTL8852AE (10ec:8852, firmware 0.13.36.2),
  Linux 7.1.5: passive capture on 2.4 and 5 GHz, aireplay-ng -9,
  injection of 10-byte ACK, 16-byte RTS, management and data frames
  with and without a radiotap rate, and 25 monitor interface
  delete/add cycles under concurrent injection. No WARN, oops or
  lockdep reports.
- Not runtime-tested on RTL8852B/C, RTL8851B, RTL8922A (BE), USB
  devices or DBCC setups. The RX filter bits changed in patch 3 have
  the same positions in R_AX_RX_FLTR_OPT and R_BE_RX_FLTR_OPT.
- The series builds with W=1 and C=1 (sparse) without new warnings.

Changes in v5:
- Split the NULL vif fix and the signed rate index fix out as
  separate patches with Fixes: tags.
- Split the previous injection patch into patches 5-9, one change
  each.
- Only send injected control frames through the management path;
  control frames built by mac80211 (e.g. BlockAckReq) keep using the
  data path as before.
- Drop rtw89_recalc_pure_monitor_vif(). mac80211 only adds the
  virtual monitor vif while no other interface is open, and removes
  it before a non-monitor interface is added, so the existing update
  rules for pure_monitor_mode_vif already give the same result. Patch
  4 is now a plain RCU conversion.
- Reword commit messages: describe the observed firmware behaviour in
  patch 5 instead of claims about firmware internals, and fix the
  description of the NULL dereference.

Changes in v4:
- Use full legal name in From/Signed-off-by.
- Retain FIF_CONTROL and FIF_PSPOLL and also clear B_AX_A_MC and
  B_AX_A_MC_LIST_CAM_MATCH in monitor mode.
- Split the RCU conversion of pure_monitor_mode_vif into its own
  patch.
- Handle injected control frames, negative rate indices, NO_ACK and
  sequence number preservation.
- Move monitor restart channel restoration into rtw89_ops_config().
- Drop the inaccurate Fixes: tag from the channel restore patch.

Changes in v3:
- Split into a patch series.
- Dropped direct register writes in favor of driver abstractions.
- Added RCU synchronization around pure_monitor_mode_vif.

